# Maintainer: Jan Alexander Steffens (heftig) <heftig@archlinux.org>
# Contributor: Eric Bélanger <eric@archlinux.org>
#
# Arch's webkit2gtk-4.1 recipe, with ppc64le added and the JavaScriptCore JIT
# port staged in prepare(). See prepare() and the powerpc64le branches of
# build() for what differs from upstream's.
#
# TREAT THE FIRST ppc64le BUILD AS A BRING-UP, NOT A REBUILD. What has been
# verified is the JSC half: the staged tree configures and builds with
# PORT=JSCOnly and runs all four JS tiers plus all three wasm tiers on POWER9,
# and prepare()'s stage.sh has been run against a pristine 2.54.1 tarball and
# reports zero residue. What has NOT been verified is this recipe end to end --
# no makepkg run has completed, and PORT=GTK has never been built on ppc64le.
# PORT=GTK additionally compiles WebCore, which is far larger than JSC and is
# what -mminimal-toc and -Wl,--no-keep-memory below exist for; expect to find
# problems there that the JSCOnly builds could not have surfaced.
#
# The installed base/webkit2gtk-4.1 is 2.50.4 and is a CLoop build with no
# ppc64 JIT symbols at all, so this is also a version bump. ours/artcraft
# depends on webkit2gtk-4.1 and is the consumer that wants the JIT.

pkgbase=webkit2gtk-4.1
pkgname=(
  webkit2gtk-4.1
  webkit2gtk-4.1-docs
)
pkgver=2.54.1
pkgrel=1
pkgdesc="Web content engine for GTK"
url="https://webkitgtk.org"
arch=(x86_64 powerpc64le)
